.TH auto-pxe-installer-setup 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-pxe-installer-setup - Configure PXE install server

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-pxe-installer-setup file.iso
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
file.iso    Name of ISO image to install
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-pxe-installer-setup
command configures a PXE installer server, utilizing dhcpd, tftpf,
and nfsd.  This server automates operating system installation
on other computers on the same network when they are booted in PXE
mode.

Primary references:
https://www.ixsystems.com/whats-new/freebsd-unattended-installation-of-servers/
man bsdinstall
https://www.wonkity.com/~wblock/docs/html/pxe.html

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-pxe-installer-setup FreeBSD-14.5-RELEASE-amd64-disc1.iso
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-pxe-boot(8), auto-pxe-node-discover(8)

